@crew v-dunmore-rhea
// Writer 4, batch 5: a short-stay visitor. Mostly not about work.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hey! Rhea Dunmore. I play the lounges. Hum me something. Anything.
- Morning! I'm only here three days. Hum quickly.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}! I played your hum last night. Everyone clapped. Mostly for the tune.   #warm
?

== chat
- One lounge at a time. I've played forty. Yours has the best curved window.
- Up early to practise. I'm told the washroom choir is the competition.   #funny

== near
? place:lounge
- Hum it. Go on. I'll play it tonight. Promise.
? time:morning
- Morning scales. Sorry, Deck 4. Lovely echo, though.   #funny
?

== bye
- {bye}. Keep humming. I'll know it if I hear it.

== smalltalk
- La la. Lovely.
- Hum it again?
